Because this environment cannot open listening sockets, I’m still driving Chromium with Playwright but fulfilling the built UI and shim HTTP routes in-process. The browser sees the same URLs, real bundled `ChatPanel`, request/response schemas, reducer, and event stream; only the loopback transport is intercepted. This keeps the protocol experiment executable and avoids substituting a mock panel.
